        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Since $s > 0$ and $c > 0$, the inequality $|\\Delta\\overline{x}_{total}| = |\\Delta\\alpha| > |\\Delta\\overline{x}_{plas}| = \\frac{s}{s+c}|\\Delta\\alpha|$ holds. This confirms the phenomenological manifestation of the evolutionary Le Chatelier's principle. Comparing Eq. (22) and Eq. (23) reveals that the final states of the phenotype and genotype are aligned $(\\Delta\\overline{x}_{total} = \\Delta\\overline{y}(\\infty) = \\Delta\\alpha)$. This indicates that genetic assimilation proceeds to eliminate the plasticity cost.",
            "block_bbox": [
                102,
